WEBVTT

00:00:04.213 --> 00:00:06.215
One, two! One, two, three!

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:33.534
Froggie went a-courtin'
and he did ride

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:37.538
Well, Froggie went a-courtin'
and he did ride

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:39.414
Somethin' Bender is great

00:00:39.498 --> 00:00:41.458
Froggie went a-courtin'
and Bender is great

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.168
Uh-huh

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.967
Oh, my God!

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.804
They dug up a bag of Olestra chips
from my time.

00:01:00.561 --> 00:01:03.313
There must be layers and layers
of old stuff down there.

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:05.983
Oh!

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.192
What's that?

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:09.528
One of those Led Zeppelins
I've heard so much about?

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:12.739
No, it's an old Volkswagen van.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.994
Hey, mister, mind if I take this old van?

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.956
Sure. You want to dump the corpses
out of theres, it's yourses.

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:23.834
Yeah, yeah. I've gotten used cars before.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.927
What's that?

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:36.597
One of those Jefferson Starships
I've heard so much about?

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.808
It's called a van. And in light of
the fact that it's not a-rockin',

00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:41.810
I invite you to come a-knockin'.

00:01:42.019 --> 00:01:43.812
Wow! Neat!

00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:46.565
It's a triumph
of free-spirited German engineering.

00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:49.526
Hey! The speedometer only goes up to 80.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.362
This thing can't go faster
than 80,000 miles an hour?

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:55.115
No, it can't. But it's got
a driver's side floor

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:58.327
and an eight-track player
with genuine mono sound.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.372
Where's the device that lets you speed
or slow the passage of time?

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:03.749
Under the seat.

00:02:07.002 --> 00:02:09.671
Why won't it start?
It just needs some gas.

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:12.716
Wrong again, idiot. There is no gas.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:16.345
Petroleum reserves ran dry in 2038.

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:18.889
Gas was an environmental disaster anyway.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.766
Now we use alternative fuels.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.351
- Like what?
- Whale oil.

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.355
Bender, lift it up to the can opener.

00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:28.732
Oh, no! I'm not going near it.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.902
Last time, that magnetic psycho
nearly cut my head off.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.946
Oh, right. Plus, the magnet

00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:36.740
screws up your inhibition unit
and makes you sing folk songs.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:40.410
What? Who said anything about me
secretly wanting to be a folk singer?

00:02:40.494 --> 00:02:42.579
How ridiculous!

00:02:42.663 --> 00:02:46.291
Bender, if you don't open that can
right now, your fear will own you.

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:49.753
And nothing that can opener could ever do
would be worse than that.

00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:52.756
Okay. Okay. I can do this.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.301
It's time to take life by the cans.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:03.308
- Come on.
- You can do it.

00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:04.810
Go on, you dummy.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:11.441
Jimmy crack corn
and I don't care

00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:14.319
Jimmy crack corn and I don't care

00:03:15.654 --> 00:03:17.281
Oh, no!

00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:20.993
I don't care 'cause the master's gone away

00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:23.579
It's toe-tappingly tragic.

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:29.918
Doc, I can't move my arms and legs.
What's wrong with me?

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:33.255
This is the worst part of the job.

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:37.801
- What is it? Good news?
- Bender, your hydraulics are shot.

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:40.304
You'll never move again.

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.556
- You mean...
- I'm sorry.

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:44.725
You'll have to get a new one.

00:03:48.103 --> 00:03:49.563
Poor Bender.

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:51.648
Well, let's drag him to the curb.

00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:54.026
Wait a minute. Bender is my best friend.

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:57.070
We can't just dump him in the gutter
like Grandma's ashes.

00:03:57.154 --> 00:04:00.616
Oh! My life is over.

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:03.911
I'll never know happiness again.

00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:06.205
Hello there.

00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:08.332
Look, Bender. It's Patch Cord Adams.

00:04:08.415 --> 00:04:10.334
He heals with the power of laughter.

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.960
Come on. Take it.

00:04:12.044 --> 00:04:14.046
What's the matter? Can't move your arms?

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:17.257
Obviously not,
or I'd be strangling you right now.

00:04:17.341 --> 00:04:19.676
Hey, here's a giggle.

00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:23.972
Did you hear why they're using
Windows 3000 as a prison guard?

00:04:24.056 --> 00:04:26.391
- No. Why?
- 'Cause it always locks up.

00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:31.772
For the love of God,
somebody kick his ass!

00:04:31.855 --> 00:04:34.816
Well, so long. Get well soon.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.278
Whoa. Well. So long anyway.

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:42.449
Oh, I'm doomed!

00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:46.036
Everybody leave me alone.
I don't wanna be seen this way.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.290
Aw, you look so sad.

00:04:50.374 --> 00:04:52.292
You want me to send
Patch Cord Adams back in?

00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:04.388
Hey, the blues.

00:05:04.471 --> 00:05:06.974
The tragic sound
of other people's suffering.

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:09.476
That's kind of a pick-me-up.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:20.571
- Wow, that was great!
- Hey, thanks. You a fan?

00:05:20.654 --> 00:05:23.240
I don't know. Let me see.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.410
Oh, my God, you're Beck!

00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:29.246
I'd get up to shake your hand
and steal your wallet,

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:32.249
but my crappy body crapped out on me.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:35.460
Don't take it so hard.
I used to miss my body, too,

00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:38.964
but then I fished this mannequin out
of the 92-Cent Store Dumpster.

00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:41.717
Wow! We've sure got a lot in common, Beck.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.262
I always dreamed of being
a musician-poet who transcends genres,

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.598
even as he reinvents them, just like you.

00:05:47.681 --> 00:05:50.434
So do it, robot.
It's easier than it looks.

00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:52.603
Yeah, thanks, but it's hopeless.

00:05:52.686 --> 00:05:54.605
I'll never be a musician now.

00:05:54.688 --> 00:05:59.818
Or maybe you'll be
the best musician ever.

00:06:07.117 --> 00:06:08.285
What's this for?

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:11.705
Try and scrape it across your chest,
like a knife on burnt toast.

00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:17.336
Come on. Move those arms.
Use the power of mental thinking.

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:18.712
Make it dynamic.

00:06:20.547 --> 00:06:23.967
Yeah! All right.
Congratulations, my friend.

00:06:24.051 --> 00:06:26.220
Why? 'Cause I can make annoying noises?

00:06:26.303 --> 00:06:29.973
Exactly. I use those
all the time in my music.

00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:33.227
Bender, I want you to become
my new washboard player.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.146
All right!

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:39.233
Go Bender! Go Bender! Go Bender!

00:06:47.324 --> 00:06:49.159
Well, that's my good friend Beck.

00:06:49.243 --> 00:06:52.829
I'm off to rock a series
of mid-level venues.

00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:56.041
Kudos, Bender.
You got mangled, and now you're a singer.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:58.085
Both our dreams came true.

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:02.214
Hey, I have an idea.
Who wants to cram in my van

00:07:02.297 --> 00:07:05.342
and follow Bender on tour
and live there in the van?

00:07:07.261 --> 00:07:11.890
I don't know, Fry. I think I'm too poor
to follow a band around in a van.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:16.186
Come on. Move it.
We gotta get to the concert

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.480
and make the audience
wait for it to start.

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:46.425
Bad news, friends.

00:07:46.508 --> 00:07:48.427
My shell ran.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.429
Zoidberg, you idiot!

00:07:50.512 --> 00:07:53.056
My outfit... It's... It's...

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.434
- Kind of cool.
- Yeah. I like it.

00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:58.562
- Me, too, now that I'm used to it.
- Then it was all on purpose.

00:07:58.645 --> 00:08:00.939
You're lucky to have Zoidberg as a friend.

00:08:01.023 --> 00:08:03.650
But cross me,
and I'll turn on you like that.

00:08:06.612 --> 00:08:09.072
There's a destination a little up the road

00:08:09.156 --> 00:08:11.867
From the habitations and the towns we know

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.411
A place we saw the lights turn low

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.747
The jigsaw jazz and the get-fresh flow

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.333
Pulling out jives and jamboree handouts

00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:21.752
Two turntables and a microphone

00:08:21.835 --> 00:08:23.795
Bottles and cans
just clap your hands

00:08:23.879 --> 00:08:25.797
Just clap your hands

00:08:25.881 --> 00:08:28.759
Where it's at

00:08:28.842 --> 00:08:31.720
Got a washboard stomach and a microphone

00:08:34.181 --> 00:08:36.475
That was a washboard brain

00:08:36.558 --> 00:08:38.936
Oh, yeah!

00:08:39.019 --> 00:08:40.479
Yeah!

00:08:40.562 --> 00:08:42.564
One bowl of Jell-O knuckles, please.

00:08:42.648 --> 00:08:45.776
That'll be three "pic-a-tures"
of George Washington.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.780
Oh, no! My beautiful money!

00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:54.034
- It got ruined in the wash.
- Mine, too. Even my change.

00:08:54.117 --> 00:08:56.328
Get lost, you moneyless hippies!

00:08:56.411 --> 00:08:58.330
You heard him, freaks.

00:08:58.413 --> 00:09:00.707
We don't like your type around here.

00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:03.544
These are the types we like.

00:09:06.129 --> 00:09:10.175
Bender, that was the best
40-minute washboard solo I've ever heard.

00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:13.220
The parts when I was awake
blew my mind.

00:09:15.722 --> 00:09:19.476
Whoa. Check out all those broken robots.
Howdy, fellas!

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.062
Oh, I don't believe my broken eyes!

00:09:22.145 --> 00:09:24.314
It's Bender, the washboard player!

00:09:24.398 --> 00:09:27.067
Hey, man, we caught your concert
from here.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.694
You rock!

00:09:28.777 --> 00:09:31.530
Oh, oh, Bender, sign my chest!

00:09:31.613 --> 00:09:33.699
It's in that bin behind me.

00:09:33.782 --> 00:09:37.327
Yo, brother! Thanks for showin'
that broken robots are still useful.

00:09:37.411 --> 00:09:39.663
Aw, hang in there, folks.

00:09:39.746 --> 00:09:42.040
I bet before you know it,
you guys'll be...

00:09:52.176 --> 00:09:56.013
That is so wrong!
You can't just melt down broken robots.

00:09:56.096 --> 00:09:58.015
Not right when they're kissing my ass.

00:09:58.098 --> 00:10:00.267
Whoa, dawg. Just cold chill.

00:10:02.019 --> 00:10:04.479
You know, when I'm upset,
I write a song about it.

00:10:04.563 --> 00:10:08.358
Like, when I wrote "Devil's Haircut,"
I was feeling really...

00:10:08.442 --> 00:10:11.236
- What's that song about?
- Hey, yeah.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:14.072
I could write a song. With real words.

00:10:14.156 --> 00:10:16.241
Not phony ones, like "odelay."

00:10:16.325 --> 00:10:19.536
"Odelay" is a word.
Just look it up in the Becktionary.

00:10:19.786 --> 00:10:20.787
Ooh.

00:10:29.046 --> 00:10:32.424
I'm workin' on my song.
Hand me the Becktionary.

00:10:32.508 --> 00:10:36.053
No, no, the rhyming Becktionary.

00:10:36.136 --> 00:10:39.389
I wish I could help
raise awareness about broken robots.

00:10:39.473 --> 00:10:42.309
But what can I do?
I only weigh eight pounds.

00:10:42.392 --> 00:10:45.229
Wait a minute.
You know lots of rock stars.

00:10:45.312 --> 00:10:48.232
And most of them like to look
like they care about things.

00:10:48.315 --> 00:10:51.902
We can all get together for
a big benefit concert in San Francisco.

00:10:51.985 --> 00:10:55.739
And we can call it "Bend-Aid"
after me, Bender.

00:10:55.822 --> 00:10:57.574
And you can sing that song you're writing.

00:10:57.658 --> 00:11:00.077
And I'll let you sing backup.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.580
But remember who the star is.
Me, Bender.

00:11:37.239 --> 00:11:41.618
All right. "Hands in the air"
rhymes with "just don't care."

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:43.954
And finished!

00:11:44.621 --> 00:11:48.166
Ugh! Smells like something
died in the wall.

00:11:48.292 --> 00:11:50.085
Surprise!

00:11:51.712 --> 00:11:53.380
Mind if we crash here tonight?

00:11:53.463 --> 00:11:55.299
The colors in the van
are keeping us awake.

00:11:55.382 --> 00:11:58.635
All right, but hands off the minibar.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:03.348
Wow! I forgot about TV.
Living free on the road,

00:12:03.432 --> 00:12:05.893
you realize how much better
life is without it.

00:12:05.976 --> 00:12:07.436
Well, let's see what's on.

00:12:08.562 --> 00:12:10.647
Tuesday, Golden Gate Park...

00:12:10.731 --> 00:12:14.026
The monsters of vaguely
folkish alterna-rock

00:12:14.109 --> 00:12:18.822
will strum your brains out
at Bend-Aid!

00:12:18.906 --> 00:12:21.658
Featuring Beck, Wailing Fungus

00:12:21.742 --> 00:12:23.785
and special guest Bender!

00:12:23.869 --> 00:12:26.288
A portion of the proceeds
might go to help broken robots.

00:12:26.371 --> 00:12:27.998
- Yeah!
- Hooray! Great.

00:12:28.081 --> 00:12:31.418
- Bender, you're famous!
- Yeah.

00:12:31.502 --> 00:12:33.420
This coming together of superstars

00:12:33.504 --> 00:12:36.548
really means a lot to you,
doesn't it, Bender?

00:12:36.632 --> 00:12:37.633
Uh-huh.

00:12:37.716 --> 00:12:39.551
Helping my defective brothers

00:12:39.635 --> 00:12:41.803
is the first thing I've ever cared about,

00:12:41.887 --> 00:12:44.139
even the slightest bit.

00:12:44.223 --> 00:12:47.601
You know, when I first got broken,

00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:51.438
I thought my life was over,
but look at me now.

00:12:51.522 --> 00:12:55.275
I got fame, money, groupies,

00:12:55.359 --> 00:12:59.196
and it's all thanks to
being completely immobilized.

00:12:59.279 --> 00:13:02.783
That's why I'll be proud
to go up on stage tomorrow and say,

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:06.620
"Look at me, world! I am a broken robot!"

00:13:06.703 --> 00:13:09.540
Bender, you can move. You're cured.

00:13:09.623 --> 00:13:13.001
Oh, crap! It's a miracle!

00:13:17.381 --> 00:13:19.216
I can move again.

00:13:20.968 --> 00:13:23.720
My music career is over.

00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:26.557
Bender, I don't claim
to understand "the biz,"

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:29.142
but wouldn't being able to move
help your music career?

00:13:29.226 --> 00:13:31.228
No! Don't you see?

00:13:31.311 --> 00:13:34.940
I was a hero to broken robots
'cause I was one of them.

00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:38.318
But how can I sing about
being damaged if I'm not?

00:13:38.402 --> 00:13:42.072
That's like Christina Aguilera
singin' in Spanish.

00:13:42.155 --> 00:13:45.993
Wait! That's it! I'll fake it.

00:13:59.131 --> 00:14:01.175
You better not do that at the concert.

00:14:01.258 --> 00:14:05.179
I can't stop. When I eat too much dirt,
I get stuff in my throat.

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:10.225
Ugh! You are so disgusting. I...

00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:14.688
They're beautiful!

00:14:14.771 --> 00:14:16.690
Ew. You're touching them.

00:14:16.773 --> 00:14:18.692
I've never seen pearls like this.

00:14:18.775 --> 00:14:20.861
Dr. Zoidberg, you're amazing!

00:14:20.944 --> 00:14:24.865
I am? At last, recognition!

00:14:29.828 --> 00:14:33.081
Gentle hippies,
put your filthy hands together

00:14:33.165 --> 00:14:36.919
for the folk stylings
of Cylon and Garfunkel!

00:14:40.506 --> 00:14:42.382
Here's a song that was beautiful

00:14:42.466 --> 00:14:44.551
when performed by my ancestor, Art.

00:14:46.053 --> 00:14:51.725
Are you goin'
to Scarborough Fair

00:14:51.808 --> 00:14:57.272
Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme

00:14:57.356 --> 00:15:00.567
Remember me

00:15:00.651 --> 00:15:03.028
To one who lives there

00:15:05.072 --> 00:15:07.324
She once was

00:15:07.407 --> 00:15:10.869
A true love of mine

00:15:10.953 --> 00:15:14.414
- We're home.
- Well, let's earn some bread.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.585
Brothers and sisters, get your love beads.

00:15:18.669 --> 00:15:21.839
Can't journey to the center of your mind
without love beads.

00:15:21.922 --> 00:15:24.550
Wow, look at the colors!

00:15:24.633 --> 00:15:26.927
These'll go great with my soul.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:31.265
Glad you like them. I've been making
fine jewelry for years, apparently.

00:15:31.348 --> 00:15:34.351
- I'll take three.
- Give me one, man.

00:15:34.434 --> 00:15:36.436
I'll trade you a bad poem.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:40.232
And now, stand up and turn on
your hidden tape recorders

00:15:40.315 --> 00:15:43.068
for Beck!

00:15:43.151 --> 00:15:46.738
With special guest,
Bender, the Broken Robot!

00:15:52.661 --> 00:15:55.664
- Bender rules!
- Groove on, man!

00:15:55.747 --> 00:15:57.749
Rock it, Bender!

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.922
Can't you hear
those cavalry drums

00:16:04.006 --> 00:16:06.884
Hijacking your equilibrium

00:16:06.967 --> 00:16:08.886
-Oh, yeah
-Midnight snacks

00:16:08.969 --> 00:16:10.888
In the mausoleum

00:16:21.315 --> 00:16:24.985
Thank you. That song doesn't
usually last three hours,

00:16:25.068 --> 00:16:27.571
but we got into a serious thing,

00:16:27.654 --> 00:16:29.573
and then I forgot how it ended.

00:16:29.656 --> 00:16:32.409
Anyway, one last item
of business before we go.

00:16:32.492 --> 00:16:36.079
Bender, to start your foundation
for broken robots,

00:16:36.163 --> 00:16:39.750
here's a big cardboard check for $14,000.

00:16:39.833 --> 00:16:42.586
It's been an emotional day for me.

00:16:42.669 --> 00:16:44.880
I don't know what to say.

00:16:44.963 --> 00:16:48.300
Then maybe you should sing it.
Lay it down, boys.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:53.639
Ladies, gentlemen,
smoking heaps of machinery...

00:16:55.516 --> 00:16:58.727
This is a song called "My Broken Friend."

00:17:02.064 --> 00:17:05.192
People say
my broken friend is useless

00:17:05.275 --> 00:17:07.569
But I say his mind is free

00:17:07.653 --> 00:17:13.242
There's lots of things
my mangled robot friend could be

00:17:13.325 --> 00:17:14.326
Kick it.

00:17:14.409 --> 00:17:16.495
He could make a good hat rack

00:17:16.578 --> 00:17:18.539
He only has to stand there

00:17:18.622 --> 00:17:21.875
-Or a cheap doorstop
-He doesn't need to move

00:17:21.959 --> 00:17:24.878
-Or a great big giant thermos
-Giant thermos

00:17:24.962 --> 00:17:28.215
-With a twist-off top
-That would be good for soup

00:17:28.298 --> 00:17:30.634
He could be a storage closet

00:17:30.717 --> 00:17:32.636
For outdated pants

00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:34.096
I like 'em tight

00:17:34.179 --> 00:17:36.974
My broken friend could do it all

00:17:37.057 --> 00:17:39.852
Just give him a chance

00:17:39.935 --> 00:17:43.480
That robot has a tragic secret

00:17:43.564 --> 00:17:45.107
That I'd like to share

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.191
For real?

00:17:46.275 --> 00:17:49.528
My broken friend is closer to me

00:17:49.611 --> 00:17:51.488
Than an ass to a chair

00:17:51.572 --> 00:17:52.573
Mmm.

00:17:52.656 --> 00:17:55.784
That robot's name I never told you

00:17:55.868 --> 00:17:56.869
Who's that?

00:17:56.952 --> 00:17:58.203
You could not foresee

00:17:58.287 --> 00:17:59.288
Come on. Give it up.

00:17:59.371 --> 00:18:02.332
I'll say it loud and sing it proud

00:18:02.416 --> 00:18:05.002
His name is you and me

00:18:05.085 --> 00:18:08.505
-Don't melt me down into a crowbar
-That suffers alone

00:18:08.589 --> 00:18:11.258
-Just 'cause I can't move my arms and legs
-Arms and legs

00:18:11.341 --> 00:18:13.135
Or toss me into a trash can

00:18:13.218 --> 00:18:14.344
Bender, what are you doing?

00:18:14.428 --> 00:18:16.513
Just 'cause I can't cook you ham and eggs

00:18:16.597 --> 00:18:17.598
What are you doing?

00:18:17.681 --> 00:18:19.391
Don't crush me into an anchor

00:18:19.474 --> 00:18:20.559
Yo, what's the dillio?

00:18:20.642 --> 00:18:23.187
Just 'cause I can't jump
and dance and sing

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:24.730
But... No. But, Bender...

00:18:24.813 --> 00:18:26.773
I'm telling you my broken friend

00:18:26.857 --> 00:18:29.359
Put your hands in the air
like you just don't care

00:18:29.443 --> 00:18:30.444
No...

00:18:30.569 --> 00:18:32.946
I'm telling you my broken friend

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:34.323
Can do most

00:18:34.406 --> 00:18:35.407
Cut it.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:36.992
Anything

00:18:37.075 --> 00:18:38.744
Cut it.

00:18:38.827 --> 00:18:40.537
- Yeah!
- Cut it!

00:18:43.457 --> 00:18:45.959
Curse my natural showmanship!

00:18:46.043 --> 00:18:49.505
You big, fat fraud!
You're not really broken!

00:18:49.588 --> 00:18:53.467
But you will be in a minute!
Bum-rush the stage!

00:18:57.804 --> 00:18:59.556
Get him!

00:19:06.813 --> 00:19:08.232
Whoa!

00:19:08.315 --> 00:19:11.610
Oh, harsh! I didn't get my beads.

00:19:14.863 --> 00:19:18.200
You, minion, lift up my arm.

00:19:18.283 --> 00:19:19.952
After him!

00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:32.714
Well, everyone, prepare to get
your guts kicked out by folk singers.

00:19:57.197 --> 00:19:59.783
What is this? The Year of the Jerk?

00:20:02.202 --> 00:20:03.829
Hurry! The Golden Gate Bridge.

00:20:03.912 --> 00:20:05.998
Put the metal to the pedal
to the other metal.

00:20:12.504 --> 00:20:15.299
Oh, no! I forgot this is a hoverbridge.

00:20:15.382 --> 00:20:17.467
And I forgot this isn't a hover car!

00:20:17.551 --> 00:20:18.886
Is any of that a problem?

00:20:18.969 --> 00:20:21.263
Not if you've lived a life without regret.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:29.146
I'll save me!

00:20:29.229 --> 00:20:31.148
Quick, grab his foot cuffs!

00:20:41.533 --> 00:20:42.743
Bummer.

00:20:45.495 --> 00:20:50.083
Someone fat get in my way!

00:20:56.715 --> 00:20:58.467
I'm broken again.

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:01.845
- I can't move any part of me.
- Good.

00:21:01.929 --> 00:21:04.223
I'm really sorry I lied, Beck.

00:21:04.306 --> 00:21:07.017
All I ever wanted
was to make music with you.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:10.145
I never meant to hurt anyone,
or help anyone.

00:21:10.229 --> 00:21:14.191
Bender, that's some played-out,
new jack horse crap.

00:21:14.274 --> 00:21:17.569
But I know you don't mean it,
so apology accepted.

00:21:17.653 --> 00:21:19.696
So, I can keep the check?

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:21.782
Over my dead career!

00:21:22.824 --> 00:21:25.118
Well, it was worth a shot.

00:21:33.293 --> 00:21:36.505
Come on, Bender! If you're done
scamming Beck, we're heading home.

00:21:36.588 --> 00:21:39.007
All right, all right.

00:21:39.091 --> 00:21:42.344
Let me just do one thing
to cheer myself up.

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:46.056
Right!

00:21:46.139 --> 00:21:48.058
Fry crack corn and I don't care

00:21:48.141 --> 00:21:50.060
Leela crack corn
I still don't care

00:21:50.143 --> 00:21:53.021
Bender crack corn and he is great

00:21:53.105 --> 00:21:55.107
Take that, you stupid corn